<title>UK: Aluminium output rose in December - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium output rose in December - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily average primary aluminium output in December 1996 rose to 51,900 tonnes compared with 51,700 in November and 48,500 in December 1995, provisional figures from the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Total production in December (31 days) was 1.608 million tonnes, compared with 1.551 million in November (30 days) and 1.505 million in December 1995.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of primary aluminium production was as follows (in thousands of tonnes) the IPAI said.</p>
<p>				Dec 96   Nov 96   Dec 95</p>
<p>    Africa		    93	 90	 68</p>
<p>    North America	  501	483	479</p>
<p>    Latin America	  178	173	179</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	148	139	140</p>
<p>    Europe West	    273	263	n/a</p>
<p>    Europe East/Central  270	263	n/a</p>
<p>    Oceania		  145	140	134</p>
</text>
